entry.summary:
About a year ago I started keeping a list. The pattern was always the same - OpenAI SDK, one API call per user message, So I spent almost an year building Sentinel Protocol and today I'm open-sourcing it. A local security proxy for LLM API calls. It sits between your application and Zero cloud calls for security decisions. Everything runs on your machine. The npx --yes --package sentinel-protocol sentinel bootstrap --profile paranoid --mode enforce --dashboard
Proxy starts at http://127.0.0.1:8787. Dashboard at http://127.0.0.1:8788. Change one line in your SDK: const openai = new OpenAI({ apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY, baseURL: 'http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1', defaultHeaders: { 'x-sentinel-target': 'openai' } });
Everything else stays identical. Your app code doesn't change. The …
